# `with object do … end` (extensions/sugar/with_blocks.warp, wiki/with.md, card with-do-block): a statement whose word takes a typed value is called on the object, any other stays as written

«class Pen { x: int }; move(p: Pen, by: int) := { p.x = p.x + by }; p = Pen(1); n = 5; with p do { move n; move 2 }; p.x»	8
«class Pen { x: int }; move(p: Pen, by: int) := { p.x = p.x + by }; p = Pen(1); with p do move 3 end; p.x»	4
# a word alone is a call without arguments; an assignment stays an assignment
«class Pen { x: int }; reset(p: Pen) := { p.x = 0 }; p = Pen(7); n = 0; with p do { reset; n = 4 }; [p.x, n]»	[0, 4]
# a typed library word too; the block's value is its last statement's
«xs = [3, 1, 2]; with xs do { sort }»	[1, 2, 3]
# the object is evaluated once
«class Pen { x: int }; move(p: Pen, by: int) := { p.x = p.x + by }; made = 0; fresh() := { global made; made += 1; Pen(made * 10) }; with fresh() do { move 1; move 2 }; made»	1
# a class's own method named with stays its own
«class Box<T>{item:T; with(x:T) := Box(x)}; Box(1).with(2).item»	2
